# Tech Stack - feature/database (Maddi Soumya)

Database Engine : SQLite (file-based, local, zero-config)
Driver / Access : Node.js built-in `node:sqlite` module (DatabaseSync) - no
                  external/native npm dependency required (Node >= 22.5.0)
Schema          : Plain SQL DDL file (database/schema.sql), applied via a
                  Node migration runner (database/migrate.js)
Seed Data       : Programmatic seed script (database/seed.js) generating
                  real relational demo records (not static JSON)
Tooling scripts : database/reset.js (drop + migrate + seed), database/verify.js
                  (row-count + business-rule sanity checks)

Why this stack:
- Fully offline/local - no database server process, no cloud account,
  no internet connection needed to build, run, or demo the app.
- Zero install friction - node:sqlite ships with Node.js itself, avoiding
  native-build tooling issues (node-gyp/Visual Studio) hit with
  better-sqlite3 on this machine.
- Still a real, dynamic, queryable relational database (not static
  JSON), satisfying the "use real-time/dynamic data sources" requirement.
- Portable schema.sql / seed.js that feature/backend (Avanti) can point
  any Node-based API layer at directly, and feature/frontend (Vyshnavi)
  can inspect with any SQLite browser while the API is being built.

Where things live:
  PeoplePay360_Team301/database/
    schema.sql   - full DDL: employees, departments, job positions,
                   working schedules, contracts (period-aware, with
                   overlap-prevention triggers), attendance, time off
                   types/allocations/requests, salary structures/rules,
                   payruns/payslips/payslip lines, payroll warnings,
                   roles/users (RBAC)
    migrate.js   - applies schema.sql to database/data/peoplepay360.db
    seed.js      - inserts demo data reproducing the README's worked
                   examples (contract resolution, leave balance flow)
    reset.js     - one-shot: wipe local db file + migrate + seed
    verify.js    - prints row counts and checks key business rules
    config.js    - central DB path configuration (PEOPLEPAY_DB_PATH env
                   override supported)
    README.md    - setup + usage instructions for the rest of the team

Local database file (git-ignored, generated per developer):
    PeoplePay360_Team301/database/data/peoplepay360.db
